            "format": "text/html",
            "value": "",
            "frametrail:name": "Recognising a ship",
            "frametrail:attributes": {
                "title": "Recognising a ship",
                "text": "&lt;p&gt;From above and from the shore, a cargo ship is identified by what does not change: the cranes on its deck, the colours of its hull and funnel. Bellingcat compares these between satellite images and ship-spotters&amp;#x27; photographs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2023/05/11/grain-trail-tracking-russias-ghost-ships-with-satellite-imagery/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Bellingcat: Grain Trail ↗&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
            }
        }
    },
